cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software archive and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "A five-axis stress-testing protocol for morphology-molecule associations: quantitative audit of compositional confounding, preprocessing fragility, and silent failures, demonstrated across four CPTAC cancer cohorts"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/WorldBMW/spatial-niche-proteome"
abstract: >-
  Executable five-axis audit protocol for pathology foundation-model to bulk-omics
  association pipelines: pooled out-of-fold inference (A1), a covariate ladder (A2),
  dictionary-source and feature-type preprocessing dependence (A3/A4), and double null
  controls (A5). Includes the six-mode silent-failure assertion suite, the synthetic
  spike-in generator and runner, and the multi-section Visium spatial validation scripts.
